## Task 1 


> ##### Instructions

1. Use a .qmd file to recreate the graphic shown below using gapminder dataset from `library(gapminder)` (get them to match as closely as you can).
    * Remove Kuwait from the data (explanation of why)
    * Use library(tidyverse) to load ggplot2 and dplyr so that you can duplicate the plot below. (Hint: use + `theme_bw()` to get the proper formatting)
    * `Use scale_y_continuous(trans = "sqrt")` to get the correct scale on the y-axis.
    
<img src="./gapminder_part_1_recreate_this.png" width=700px>

> ##### Plot Recreation (*My Work*)

<!--  
  1) Data Cleaning, 
  2) Graphic Recreation 
-->
```{r}
#| label: "Plot Recreation"
#| fig-width: 10
#| fig-height: 4

# 1) Data Cleaning:
#     • Remove Kuwait 
#     • Change the scale of `pop` (population) to 100k.
gap2 <- gap %>% 
  filter(country != "Kuwait") %>% 
  mutate(
    pop_k = pop / 100000
  )


# 2) Recreated Plot
ggplot(gap2, aes(x = lifeExp, y = gdpPercap)) +
    labs(
    x = "Life Expectancy",
    y = "GDP per Capita",
    size = "Population (100k)",
    color = "Continent"
  ) +
  geom_point(aes(size = pop_k, color = continent), alpha = 0.8) +
  facet_wrap(~ year, nrow = 1) +
  scale_y_continuous(trans = "sqrt") +
  scale_size_continuous(range = c(.2, 3)) +
  theme_bw() +
  theme(
    axis.text = element_text(size = 6),
    axis.title = element_text(size = 10),

    legend.title = element_text(size = 9),
    legend.text = element_text(size = 7),
    legend.key.size = unit(0.45, "cm"),
    legend.spacing.y = unit(0.1, "cm")
  ) +
  guides(
    size = guide_legend(override.aes = list(size = c(1, 2, 3, 4, 5))),
    color = guide_legend(override.aes = list(size = 3))
  )
```





